🔹 CONCEPT 2: PRIORITY QUEUE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Elements are dequeued based on PRIORITY, not arrival order.

Types:
• Min Priority Queue - Smallest element has highest priority
• Max Priority Queue - Largest element has highest priority

Implementation: Usually using Heap (not array)

Applications:
- Dijkstra's shortest path
- Huffman coding
- Task scheduling
- Event-driven simulation

🔹 CONCEPT 3: CIRCULAR DEQUE
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Combination of circular queue and deque.
Allows insertion/deletion at both ends with circular nature.

Full Condition: (rear + 1) % capacity == front
Empty Condition: front == -1

